% Every exam keeps each page's outer top corner free for the cut-off tab of printed student copies (issue #211): a guillotine through a long-edge duplex or
% booklet stack cuts it, top right on odd pages and top left on even ones; the header mirrors on even pages. One layout for every exam, so the OMR template never
% depends on how a sheet was printed. The reserved zone (an 86.6 x 23.1 mm triangle per corner) is mirrored in frontend lib/qr/cutCorner.ts, which draws the tab and covers it on scans.

\newcounter{Punkte}
